  "comparability": "CMS Medicare and Medicaid are NHEA source-of-funds program totals including administration and applicable private-plan non-medical costs; Medicaid (Title XIX) excludes separately tabulated CHIP and CMS deducts Medicaid Medicare-premium buy-ins to avoid double counting. VA health care is CMS's Department of Veterans Affairs NHEA measure: VA-supplied detailed quarterly expenditure categories converted to calendar-year totals and mapped to NHE service categories. It represents VHA care and associated administration, not the whole VA budget. NHEA VA spending and Medicare/Medicaid financing totals are not identical kinds of delivery or populations. CMS 2024 vintage includes comprehensive historical revisions. BEA GDP is a later vintage (published 2026-10-29); its 2024 GDP is compared with CMS summary GDP and small revision-vintage differences are recorded. The GDP share uses BEA nominal GDP for each matching calendar year; the real-dollar series uses BEA GDP implicit price deflator, latest common year 2024. Deflation adjusts general economy-wide prices, not healthcare-specific prices or service volume."
